> The letter "c" is not used in finnish, and the book speaks about orcs
> all the time so it would have looked quite stupid to leave it
> untranslated, IMO.

Something like that. Even though 'c' isn't used in Finnish words, it
exists in the alphabet, but when a word is used so often, it is a good
idea to translate it so that it sounds better.

Most substantives in Finnish end with a wovel, and many borrowed words
have been basically formed by just adding 'i' to the end and duplicating
the consonant before it. And when you translate anyway, it's logical to
change 'c' to 'k' to make it look more natural in Finnish.
And in this case, changing the initial o to ö makes it sound better, IMHO.

